---
fetch something once, without a project

usage: fetchloom get [options] <link>...

arguments:
  [link]...  what to download: search words, a link, a DOI, or an id such as
             zenodo:3608990. several links download together, so search words in
             quotes go alone

options:
  -o, --output <dir>       put the download in <dir> instead of a new folder
                           named after it. with several links, each gets its own
                           folder inside <dir>
  -i, --input-file <file>  read links from <file>, one a line, or from stdin for
                           -. blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped
      --sha256 <hex>       check the file's SHA-256 before placing it. needs one
                           link to one file
      --select <glob>      keep only files matching this pattern, such as
                           "**/*.csv". repeat it for more
      --exclude <glob>     leave out files matching this pattern. repeat it for
                           more
      --no-extract         keep zip and tar archives packed instead of unpacking
                           them
  -q, --quiet              print only the answer, warnings and errors
  -v, --verbose...         say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug
                           logs
      --json               print one JSON document on stdout instead of the
                           story
      --offline            use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes                approve confirmations, but never choose a dataset for
                           you
      --color <when>       when to use color: auto, the default, always or never
  -C <dir>                 run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
  -h, --help               print help

examples:
  fetchloom get iris
  fetchloom get https://huggingface.co/datasets/scikit-learn/iris -o iris
  fetchloom get zenodo:3608990 figshare:34744689@1 -o downloads
  fetchloom get -i links.txt

on disk: writes one output folder for each link through the cache. does not
create project files

docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom/user/commands/get.html
